{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For My name's sake.</b> That you be called the people of HaShem." "<b>I will be patient with you.</b> It has no parallel [in Scripture], and in the words of the ancients it is חוטם (wrath), and so it is: \"I will lengthen My nose,\" and \"I will lengthen חוטם (wrath) for you,\" also \"for the sake of delaying,\" and likewise it is \"and for My praise's sake.\""], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:32.901223895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}